From f14ce6c9b80100f9df61c8b37dce2a5a718a2043 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WWE13 Recomp <wwe13-recomp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:01:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] apple: never MAP_FIXED over a live mapping; rex_smoke
 platform smoke test

memory_posix (Darwin): Memory::MapViews first tries base 1<<32, where the
arm64 main executable sits right above __PAGEZERO; MAP_FIXED would replace
the running program's own code. MapFileView now refuses occupied fixed
ranges on Darwin, and MapViews moves on to the next base.

tests/smoke (rex_smoke): opens a window through the platform backend,
presents with Vulkan (MoltenVK on Apple) and draws an ImGui overlay over a
test pattern; initializes the real guest memory layout and checks that MMIO
loads/stores trap into their callbacks (SIGBUS on Darwin). Shows size, DPI,
fullscreen, fps and input events; --smoke_seconds=N prints PASS/FAIL and
sets the exit code. Built with REXGLUE_BUILD_TESTS (Vulkan builds).
---
 src/core/memory_posix.cpp  |  10 +
 tests/CMakeLists.txt       |   3 +
 tests/smoke/CMakeLists.txt |  29 +++
 tests/smoke/smoke_app.cpp  | 444 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 486 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tests/smoke/CMakeLists.txt
 create mode 100644 tests/smoke/smoke_app.cpp

diff --git a/src/core/memory_posix.cpp b/src/core/memory_posix.cpp
index 9138b02..9da80b4 100644
--- a/src/core/memory_posix.cpp
+++ b/src/core/memory_posix.cpp
@@ -502,6 +502,16 @@ void* MapFileView(FileMappingHandle handle, void* base_address, size_t length, P
   // The emulator reserves address space first, then maps file views into it.
   // MAP_FIXED_NOREPLACE would fail with EEXIST in this case.
   if (base_address) {
+#if REX_PLATFORM_MAC
+    // On Apple silicon the main executable (and dyld's shared region) is mapped right above the
+    // 4 GB __PAGEZERO, where Memory::MapViews makes its first attempt: MAP_FIXED there would
+    // silently replace the running program's own code. Refuse occupied ranges instead; MapViews
+    // then tries the next base address.
+    if (IsRangePartlyMapped(base_address, length)) {
+      errno = EEXIST;
+      return nullptr;
+    }
+#endif
     flags |= MAP_FIXED;
   }
 
